Proves per-thread cell LAYOUT, INITIALIZATION and ADDRESSING (SPEC §11.11), not
rooting. A `@threadlocal` cell can never hold a root: #1402's untraced-type rule
makes `@threadlocal let s: string` E0082, so a traced reference cannot exist in
one, and the collector never scans these cells by construction. The program is
also straight-line — codegen emits `bit_rt_safepoint` only at loop back-edges —
so it reaches zero safepoints and a stack walk would observe nothing either way.
Its evidence is the linked binary's arithmetic on the thread pointer.
